# Paths `tauri dev`'s file watcher must NOT rebuild the application for.
#
# The watcher follows every workspace crate this binary depends on — which is most of them — and
# a rebuild here is not cheap: it relinks the app, restarts the process, and so tears down the
# tddy-daemon it hosts, every open session, every RPC connection and the log files they write.
#
# Generated trees inside those crates therefore have to be excluded by hand. `tddy-tool-engine`'s
# acceptance tests write a whole fake checkout under `tests/fixtures/buildbox-root/` (gitignored),
# so a plain `cargo test -p tddy-tool-engine` in this worktree restarted a running desktop app
# mid-session — the rebuild announced itself as
# `File .../tests/fixtures/.../hello.txt changed. Rebuilding application...`.
#
# Keep this list to things no source change can hide behind: test fixtures, scratch dirs and
# build output. Excluding a real source path would leave the app silently running stale code.

# Test fixtures, including the generated checkouts acceptance tests build inside them.
**/tests/fixtures/

# Session state, logs and scratch space a running dev stack writes continuously.
tmp/
**/tmp/
**/.tddy/

# Build output and dependencies.
target/
**/target/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/storybook-static/
